 # Voxel Grid Generation & Expansion
-Also called: Occupancy Grid Expansion, Smoke Voxelization
 
 ## Overview
-This method generates a 3D occupancy grid representing a volumetric smoke cloud by expanding a spherical radius from a central origin point over time [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of creating a discrete, GPU-friendly voxel representation for ray-marched volumetric rendering without using particle systems or billboard geometry [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from standard point-splatting by evaluating a continuous sphere falloff against a discrete grid, and from [DCX Pipeline](3770-dcx-pipeline.md) by its procedural, time-driven expansion rather than static file parsing.
